the Classical era, an age of empires, philosophical inquiry, and foundational civilizations, active in Nishapur. Known in the fields of scientists & inventors.", "newValue": "Aḥmad Ibn-Muḥammad al-Maidānī, a prominent Persian lexicographer and literary scholar who died in 1124 CE, was a pivotal figure in the preservation and systematization of classical Arabic proverbs. Operating from Nishapur, a vibrant intellectual hub during the Seljuk period, al-Maidānī’s extensive scholarship contributed significantly to the philological traditions of the Islamic Golden Age. His work provided an invaluable resource for understanding the linguistic nuances, cultural values, and historical context embedded within the vast corpus of Arabic popular wisdom.

His magnum opus, *Majmaʿ al-Amthāl* (Collection of Proverbs), stands as an monumental achievement, compiling over 6,000 Arabic proverbs organized alphabetically. Beyond mere recitation, al-Maidānī meticulously provided the historical context, origin stories, and grammatical explanations for each entry, often referencing classical Arabic poetry and historical anecdotes. This comprehensive approach distinguished his collection, transforming it from a simple compilation into a foundational reference work for Arabists and literary scholars throughout the centuries. He also authored other works, though *Majmaʿ al-Amthāl* remains his most celebrated and enduring contribution.

